  "assessment": "Independent source-closure review against the frozen arXiv TeX confirms the complete submitted RILW family. Frozen-source lines 185-197 define the rate-induced Levy-walk model and R(v)=(1/tau0)|v/v_r|^alpha with the source choices v_r=tau0=1 and alpha=2 or 4; lines 250-257 fix IID post-collision velocities with f(v)=1/2 on (-1,1). Lines 437-453 give the long-time law MSD(t) proportional to t^gamma(alpha), with gamma=2-2/alpha for alpha>3/2; lines 464-475 therefore give gamma=1 at alpha=2 and gamma=1.5 at alpha=4. The authored readout M(r)=lim_{t_ref->infinity} MSD(r*t_ref)/MSD(t_ref) is a faithful amplitude-free consequence at fixed finite r: the source prefactor cancels, yielding exactly r and r^1.5. The finite public interval r in [1,10] is a conservative benchmark subset, not a claimed source acquisition range. Independent execution on 10,001 evenly spaced r values per branch matched those two formulas with zero floating-point discrepancy, stayed finite and strictly increasing, and reproduced every diagnostic and hidden prediction exactly. The two source branches share the same public RILW apparatus, control, readout, asymptotic condition, and Identification skeleton; physical alpha=2/4 remains in branch-private fixed conditions. Historical and counterfactual public definitions are identical after normalizing the opaque instance ID in both tracks. Known-truth submissions passed all four historical/counterfactual by Identification/Discovery cells with zero held-out error, and repeated Oracle evaluation is deterministic because it returns the exact source-derived asymptotic ratio. No unresolved source, asymptotic-semantics, formula, direction, public/private-boundary, prediction, or four-cell issue remains.",
